    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters July 30th prioritizing high-upside matchups against mediocre arms, headlined by **James Wood**, who commands our highest score of the day (73.98). Facing G. Holmes, **James Wood** benefits from a massive 17% boost in SP skill projection and an elite .423 xwOBA, locking him in as a must-start. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants strong consideration (64.52); despite a slight park penalty, his excellent BvP history against Pallante and the premium value provided by his #2 spot in the order keep him firmly in the green. Meanwhile, **Josh Naylor** (65.47) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (64.03) provide the core power foundation, both capitalizing on favorable park factors and the 100% recency weight to mitigate the challenge posed by Roki Sasaki and Gray, respectively.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Cole Young**, whose score of 52.73 sits in the marginal-to-strong transition zone. While his raw base projection is modest, the optimizer favored his leadoff placement and the specific situational boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which historically creates high-probability theft environments for aggressive baserunners. Because we are hyper-focused on maintaining our standing in the scarce SB category, **Cole Young** was preferred over other depth options, though he remains a player to monitor closely if the lineup confirms him further down the order. \n\nConversely, **Dalton Rushing** is a significant risk factor today. His score of 44.69 barely clears the bench threshold, hampered by a projected #9 spot and a challenging matchup against Bryan Woo. We are currently proceeding with an assumed lineup; should **Dalton Rushing** be scratched or moved into a defensive-sub role, we will pivot immediately to preserve our daily game caps. With **Corbin Carroll** and **Mickey Moniak** sidelined by schedule voids and **Trevor Story** remaining on the IL, we are navigating a thin bench. We remain confident that the aggressive weighting toward SB-threats in the lineup, particularly with **James Wood** and **Seiya Suzuki** setting the table, will keep our Roto standing stable heading into the weekend.",
